  "steps": [
    "Garlic parm: whisk the olive oil, vinegar, garlic powder, oregano, onion powder, crushed red pepper, truffle salt, pepper, honey and Parmesan in a zip-top bag or bowl.",
    "Sweet: whisk the olive oil, balsamic, soy sauce, Worcestershire, salt, pepper, garlic, rosemary, brown sugar, lemon juice and Dijon until the sugar dissolves.",
    "Tomato: whisk the olive oil, tomato paste, lemon zest and juice, garlic, salt, pepper, smoked paprika, oregano, thyme and cayenne.",
    "All three: add 1.5 lb chicken to each marinade, turn to coat, and refrigerate at least 2 hours or up to overnight.",
    "Heat the oven to 400°F and line sheet pans with parchment. Lay the chicken out in a single layer, letting excess marinade drip off.",
    "Bake 30-40 minutes, until the thickest piece reads 165°F. Rest 5 minutes before slicing."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The creator gives the teaspoon spice amounts for the garlic parm marinade only; the oil, vinegar, honey and Parmesan amounts and the other two marinades are filled from comparable published marinades.",
    "Chicken breasts are usually done near 30 minutes; thighs take the longer end.",
    "The sugar and honey marinades brown fast; parchment keeps them from sticking and scorching."
  ],
